### EasyPark Platform API - manual requests (JetBrains Rider / VS Code REST Client)
@host = http://localhost:8080
@api = {{host}}/api/v1

### 1. Liveness and readiness
GET {{host}}/health/live

###
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### 2. Sign up a driver
POST {{api}}/authentication/sign-up
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "driver.test@easypark.local", "password": "Password123!", "role": "DRIVER" }

### 3. Sign in (copy the "token" of the response into @token)
POST {{api}}/authentication/sign-in
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "driver.test@easypark.local", "password": "Password123!" }

###
@token = PASTE_THE_TOKEN_HERE

### 4. Create the profile of the driver
POST {{api}}/profiles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Ana", "lastName": "Prueba", "phone": "+51 999 111 222" }

### 5. Register a vehicle
POST {{api}}/vehicles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "plateNumber": "XYZ-321", "vehicleType": "CAR", "color": "Azul", "isDefault": true }

### 6. Search active facilities (driver)
GET {{api}}/parking-facilities?onlyAvailable=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Reserve (the platform assigns a compatible spot)
POST {{api}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "vehicleId": 2, "parkingFacilityId": 1, "startAt": "2030-01-01T15:00:00Z", "durationMinutes": 60 }

### 8. My reservations
GET {{api}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Cancel reservation 1
PUT {{api}}/reservations/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "CANCELLED" }

### 10. Operator: register an entry (sign in as an operator first)
POST {{api}}/access-movements
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "parkingFacilityId": 1, "plateNumber": "ABC-123", "movementType": "ENTRY", "registrationMethod": "MANUAL" }
